    "comment_count": 2,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "If I understand the question correctly, you want to be able to pick any color scheme via `:Pick colorschemes` and have it automatically loaded during startup?\r\n\r\nIf yes, then this is out of scope of the picker, I am afraid. The reason is that setting color scheme is a part of user's config and can be done in various places and methods.\r\n\r\nThe suggestion here is to manually explore and pick color scheme via the picker and manually adjust 'init.lua' / config by putting a line `vim.cmd('colorscheme picked-colorscheme-name')` in it.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">If I understand the question correctly, you want to be able to pick any color scheme via <code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick colorschemes</code> and have it automatically loaded during startup?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If yes, then this is out of scope of the picker, I am afraid. The reason is that setting color scheme is a part of user's config and can be done in various places and methods.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The suggestion here is to manually explore and pick color scheme via the picker and manually adjust 'init.lua' / config by putting a line <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.cmd('colorscheme picked-colorscheme-name')</code> in it.</p>",
            "bodyText": "If I understand the question correctly, you want to be able to pick any color scheme via :Pick colorschemes and have it automatically loaded during startup?\nIf yes, then this is out of scope of the picker, I am afraid. The reason is that setting color scheme is a part of user's config and can be done in various places and methods.\nThe suggestion here is to manually explore and pick color scheme via the picker and manually adjust 'init.lua' / config by putting a line vim.cmd('colorscheme picked-colorscheme-name') in it.",
